<statement>
<p>
	This program prompts the current player to choose a move on the Tic-Tac-Toe game board.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>You will need MATLAB's</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>input</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>command to prompt the current player to choose a space.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Once the current player picks a space, your code should check if the chosen move is invalid (i.e., they chose an occupied space or one that is outside the 1-9 range). Since the player can enter multiple invalid moves, you will need a while-loop to continue asking the player for a valid space.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Once the current player selects a valid, add their move to the game state matrix and return this new game state.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
